      "message": "Let a projection change only what the log said\n\nA rebuild of the projections is a replay of the log, and every row it\nproduces has to be a row the log explains. The transfer arm broke that:\nsince change 106 it revoked every grant on a repository whose transfer\nit applied, which was right for a transfer accepted after revocations\nbecame events of their own — those events do the revoking, and the arm\nfound nothing left — and wrong for the one transfer already on the\nrecord, which the rebuild to schema 29 replayed without any such event.\nThe runner's grant to verify on the forge's own repository came out of\nthat rebuild revoked, and so did two others, with nothing in the log\nsaying so, and fsck could not see it because a replay and the live\nprojection agreed with each other and disagreed with the log.\n\nThe arm now changes nothing. Schema 30 rebuilds the projection so the\ngrants stand as the log has them, and a rehearsal on a copy of the\nflagship checks that a revoked row is never more than the revoking\nevents can account for.\n\nChange-Id: Iprojection0107\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
